WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.379
Marvel's insanely popular Black Panther was
packed with amazing moments for newcomers

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.460
and comic fans alike.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.900
But there were a few details that only the
biggest Black Panther fans truly understood.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.240
"What do you know about Wakanda?"

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.340
Warning: spoilers ahead ...

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.280
Memorial mountain

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.180
As his father T'Chaka's appearance early in
the film showed, T'Challa's Black Panther

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.480
is just one of a long lineage of super-powered
Wakandan protectors — and while T'Challa

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.000
is the most well-known Panther, Bashenga is
one of the greatest and oldest in that line.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.740
In the comics, Bashenga was one of the first
to don the garb and name of the Black Panther,

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:42.280
and the originator of both Wakanda's isolationist
leanings and the religion of the Panther God.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.380
In the Black Panther movie, Bashenga is subtly
referenced with the name of the mountain over

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.660
which the mound of Vibranium is stored: Mt.
Bashenga.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.920
Cutting-room costume

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.860
Concept art from Marvel's Black Panther: The
Art of the Movie showed T'Challa's smart-aleck

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.170
sister Shuri decked out in a vibranium Black
Panther suit herself, with the same gauntlet

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.820
she ended up wearing in the actual climax
of the film.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.920
From the concept art, it seems like the Black
Panther creators were interested in at least

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:14.110
hinting at the comics storyline in which Shuri
takes over as the Black Panther and Queen

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:14.720
of Wakanda.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.640
There may be a winking reference to that storyline
in the actual movie itself as well.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.420
On T'Challa's challenge day, Shuri is the
one who raises her hand for the right to challenge

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.300
him for the throne of Wakanda; a moment that's
played for laughs when it's revealed that

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.300
she was just tired of wearing an uncomfortable
outfit.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.480
A new Nakia

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.740
While every character in the movie is changed
at least slightly from their comics origins,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.860
the character of Nakia is almost a completely
different character.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:46.140
In the comics, the Dora Milaje were T'Challa's
brides-in-waiting, bodyguards that were betrothed

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.660
to the king indefinitely unless he were to
actively choose them.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.820
Accordingly, the comics version of Nakia was
a Dora Milaje who became obsessed with T'Challa

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.060
to the point of becoming the mind-controlling
villainess Malice.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.140
In the movie, Nakia is brave, selfless, and
T'Challa's romantic equal rather than a spurned

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:08.509
lovelorn teenager, so you would be forgiven
for thinking that the filmmakers kept nothing

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:09.240
but the name.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:14.920
Still, there's a nod toward her Dora Milaje
comics roots when Nakia dons Dora Milaje armor

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.920
for the final battle.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.160
Soldier or Wolf?

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.300
As foreshadowed in the Infinity War prequel
comics, the second post-credits sequence in

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:29.010
Black Panther showed Bucky in Wakanda, seemingly
cured of his brain-washing, with kids nearby

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.860
calling him "the White Wolf."

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.800
In the comics, Hunter, the White Wolf, is
Wakanda's spymaster, as well as T'Challa's

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.340
caucasian adopted brother.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.700
Connecting one caucasian former spy in Bucky
to the White Wolf could be just a fun reference,

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.880
or it could be establishing where Bucky will
be spending his time following the conclusion

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.260
of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.740
Maybe there's a new superhero identity for
our favorite brainwashed super spy once he

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.560
hangs up the Winter Soldier duds.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.620
Pan-African unity

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.960
When T'Challa, Nakia, and Okaye enter the
casino in South Korea to capture Klaue, it's

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.880
the start of one of the best-looking action
sequences of the movie.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.720
But one excellent detail is kind of hidden:
Nakia is dressed in all green, Okaye in all

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.870
red, and T'Challa is wearing his characteristic
black, and together their color scheme matches

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.140
the Pan-African Flag.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.640
Considering that one of the defining themes
of the movie is banding together beyond tribal

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.800
barriers, it's a beautiful way of depicting
that theme through three different characters

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.600
who band together to do what's right.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.800
Thanks for watching!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.180
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.340
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

